{"box":[-6,-35,15.1,0.5,46,3.5],"m":"steel"},{"box":[2,-35,15.1,0.5,46,3.5],"m":"steel"},{"box":[10,-35,15.1,0.5,46,3.5],"m":"steel"},{"box":[18,-35,15.1,0.5,46,3.5],"m":"steel"},{"cut":[-42,-36,18.2,64,48,2]}],"notes":"The Yuz Museum on Shanghai's West Bund (Sou Fujimoto, 2014): former Longhua Airport aircraft hangar (about 64 by 48 m here) with a shallow barrel vault on steel trusses, a clerestory glass band under the vault, concrete pilasters along its north and west flanks, and Fujimoto's glass hall wrapping it in an L under one thin white roof, with an open courtyard where the olive tree stands. Refined (3 rounds): vault re-stepped in 14 fine courses with truss ribs every 8 m; clerestory is now glass instead of a dark ledge; hall raised to 10 m, mullions every 2.5 m, thinner roof; pilasters slimmer and on two sides; courtyard opened so the olive shows. Footprint, bearing and outer walls unchanged. Still guessed: vault rise, hall height, pilaster rhythm, plaza planting. No photographs available."}